    "result": "Excellent! The feature is complete and fully tested. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Implementation Complete \u2705\n\n### 1. **`renderSummary()` function** (`src/gate/report.ts`)\n- Exports a new function that generates a one-line summary: `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>`\n- Total is always 7 (number of GATE_CHECKS)\n- Answered is the count of checks with no block-severity findings\n- Block findings are listed in GATE_CHECKS order (e.g., `BLOCK 5/7: evaluation, transparency`)\n- Special case: if gate section is missing, returns `BLOCK 0/7: structure`\n\n### 2. **`--summary` CLI flag** (`src/cli.ts`)\n- Added to `frai-gate check <spec.md>` command\n- Prints only the summary line instead of the full report\n- Exit codes remain correct (1 on BLOCK, 0 otherwise)\n- `--json` flag takes priority if both are specified\n- Updated HELP text with documentation and example\n\n### 3. **Comprehensive tests** (`src/gate/report.test.ts`)\n- 8 tests covering all scenarios:\n  - PASS verdict with no findings\n  - WARN verdict with warnings only\n  - BLOCK verdict with single and multiple findings\n  - Block findings sorted in GATE_CHECKS order\n  - Warnings don't reduce the answered count\n  - Structure issue special case\n  - Agent and validator source findings\n\n### 4. **Export** (`src/index.ts`)\n- Function is exported from the package for public use\n\nAll tests pass and the build completes successfully. The CLI is ready for use:\n```bash\nfrai-gate check FRAI-SPEC.md --summary\n# Output: PASS 7/7\n```",
